# Use a quiz to find and repair a knowledge gap — learner brief

Fictional Northstar Services training material.

## Procurement P1–P5, September 2026
P1: Requester records business need.
P2: Procurement issues approved purchase order.
P3: Receiving records receipt.
P4: AP matches invoice to order and receipt; missing receipt goes to AP exception queue.
P5: Treasury releases payment only after separate authorized approval.
Glossary: purchase order = purchasing instruction; receipt = evidence of delivery; invoice = supplier payment request; payment approval = separate authority to release funds.
Owner: Procurement Operations. No thresholds or holiday calendar supplied.

Quiz themes: order, ownership, missing receipt, matching versus payment approval.

## Task

Before joining a close-process meeting, test your understanding of the same P1–P5 process.

## Actions


1. Provide P1–P5 to AI and request four questions with answers withheld.
2. Answer without consulting the reference; mark uncertainty instead of asking for hints.
3. Ask AI for feedback tied to P1–P5.
4. Check each correction yourself and explain why one initial answer was incomplete; if all were correct, add a harder handoff question.
5. Write a next-day recall prompt that can be used without the original chat.


## Output
Four questions; initial answers; source-based corrections; one-day revisit plan.
